; The river crossing's two claims, re-asked as derivations (extension §2).
;
; This file exists to be CHECKED AGAINST river.claims, not to replace it:
; `pol check` answers `solvable` and `no-blunders` with the checker's own CTL
; reading, and `modality-cross-check.sh` re-asks the same two questions of the
; rules engine. Two implementations of one question; a disagreement is a bug in
; one of them.
;
; POLARITY — read this before "fixing" anything below.
;   `possible F` is encoded POSITIVELY: the relation holds the reachable
;   situations that satisfy F, so NON-EMPTY means the property holds.
;   `live F` is AG EF F, and no stratified Datalog relation can say "for all"
;   positively (extension §3 forbids a nullary relation, so there is nowhere to
;   put the answer). It is therefore encoded as its COUNTEREXAMPLE SET: the
;   reachable situations from which no F-situation is reachable. EMPTY means the
;   property holds. Turning `no-blunders` into "the situations that can still
;   finish" would read as the satisfying set and silently invert the oracle —
;   every `live` verdict would come out backwards while the script stayed green.

; Reachability over REAL edges only, reflexive at every situation — the same
; graph `Space.bwd_reach` walks (a gap edge has no successor, so `edge` omits
; it, and a gap exit is a non-F terminal for both implementations).
(relation reach 2)
(rule (reach S S) (situation S))
(rule (reach S T) (edge E S M) (reach M T))

; `possible`: the arrangements, reachable from the initial one, in which
; everything is across intact. Non-empty ⟺ `holds solvable`.
(relation solvable 1)
(rule (solvable T)
  (init S)
  (reach S T)
  (holds T (and (is farmer.at right) (is wolf.at right)
                (is goat.at right)   (is cabbage.at right))))

; `live`: the counterexample set. `intact` is F; `can-still-finish` is EF F;
; `no-blunders` is the reachable situations where EF F fails — the blunders.
; Non-empty ⟺ `fails no-blunders`.
(relation intact 1)
(rule (intact T)
  (situation T)
  (holds T (and (is farmer.at right) (is wolf.at right)
                (is goat.at right)   (is cabbage.at right))))

(relation can-still-finish 1)
(rule (can-still-finish S) (reach S T) (intact T))

(relation no-blunders 1)
(rule (no-blunders S) (situation S) (not (can-still-finish S)))
